Attribution
-----------

The Bitwarden vault format (KDF ladder, HKDF-stretched master key, the
`{type}.{base64 parts}` EncString envelope) and the Bitwarden server API
surface used here (`/identity/accounts/prelogin`, `/identity/connect/token`,
`/api/sync`, `/api/config`) are implemented from their public descriptions.

The design of this client is informed by **rbw** — an unofficial Bitwarden CLI
by Jesse Luehrs, MIT licensed, <https://github.com/doy/rbw>. rbw is a clean
derivation reference under this repository's licensing policy
(`docs/competitors/REUSE.md`, constitution C3): permissively licensed, so
deriving from it with attribution is allowed. This crate does not depend on
rbw and does not vendor its code; the debt is architectural — which endpoints
matter, how the key ladder is sequenced, and which envelope types a consume
client actually has to handle.

No source is copied from AGPL/GPL projects. In particular, nothing here is
taken from vaultwarden (AGPL-3.0) or from Bitwarden's own clients or server
(AGPL-3.0 / GPL-3.0). `deny.toml` mechanically enforces the permissive-only
dependency policy for the Rust side.

